Subject: [PATCH] Tier 3.5: x402Settlement assertions verify the full 402 loop
 on the mirror node

Acceptance contracts can now flag an assertion with x402Settlement. When
set, the Tier 3.5 validator prompt gains an x402 settlement-verification
block: 402 requirements, X-PAYMENT retry, and the settlement record fetched
from the mirror node - including the critical x402 distinction that the
facilitator (feePayer), not the end-user signer, is the transaction payer.
Also adds the mirror transactions endpoint (dash-form id note) to the
on-chain verification recipe, documents the flag in authoring-a-recipe.md,
and covers detection + prompt rendering with tests.
